issues.body:
Hexalith.Agents Story 5.4 and later identity/review consumers are blocked on the Parties-owned `EXT-PARTIES-1` record. See [the complete register contract](https://github.com/Hexalith/Hexalith.Agents/blob/main/_bmad-output/planning-artifacts/external-dependency-register.md#ext-parties-1--agent-party-identity-contract). Current Parties detail exposes type and active state, but the public query has no stable `AuthenticatedHumanActorId`, binding version, validity interval, or historical binding lookup.

**Product and Parties decision required:** formally select Branch A (new AI Party type and Agents-only create authority) or Branch B (approve the existing Organization-typed provisioned Party for V1). Neither branch is selected by current code. Both require immutable deterministic identity-by-id, tenant-scoped create-only provisioning under the Agents Service Principal, exact idempotent retries, typed divergent conflict, no tenant-role replacement, and no Party PII in public results. AI type verification is additional only for Branch A.

Independent of the branch, the same accepted target must expose tenant-scoped authoritative Party-by-id classification, current active/liveness, evidence position/observed instant, and typed missing/ambiguous/stale/denied/unavailable. Human Parties also need stable non-PII actor ID, binding version and validity interval, plus queryable history that reproduces the binding at an action instant. Typed missing, overlapping, ambiguous, stale, and actor-mismatch cases must fail closed; non-human Parties cannot be Approvers.

For register acceptance, please reply with:
- explicit Product and Parties Maintainer acceptance of A or B, plus the final public members and typed outcomes;
- one immutable package version or full commit for the **complete** identity and actor-binding target;
- an accepted target integration date;
- the exact executable clean-checkout compatibility command and live Level 4 evidence covering current/historical binding, cross-tenant denial, and provisioning conflict, with Level 5 requirements acknowledged.

Branch-B-compatible Agents development is permitted by the register but does not establish launch evidence or make this record Available.
